-- title:
--   Chebyshev's lower bound for the prime counting function
-- statement:
--   There are $c>0$ and $x_0$ such that for all real $x\ge x_0$,
--   $$
--   \pi(\lfloor x\rfloor)\ge\frac{c\,x}{\log x},
--   $$
--   where $\pi(n)$ is the number of primes at most $n$.
--
--   The number of primes up to $x$ is at least a constant multiple of $x/\log x$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/BinaryEdit/PrimeSupply.lean#L11-L33

